From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wbemprox: Win32_Process and Win32_Service with their properties and methods

Win32_Process gains CreationDate, HandleCount, Kernel/UserModeTime, Min/MaximumWorkingSetSize, PageFaults, PageFileUsage, Peak*, Priority, PrivatePageCount, SessionId, VirtualSize, CSName, OSName, WindowsVersion and the NULL Status/InstallDate/TerminationDate; the command line of other processes; property names ProcessId and ParentProcessId; methods Terminate, SetPriority, GetOwnerSid, and GetOwner for any process. Win32_Service gains Caption, Description, PathName, StartName, Started, ErrorControl, DesktopInteract, ExitCode, CheckPoint, WaitHint, TagId, DelayedAutoStart, Status; methods Create, Change, ChangeStartMode, Delete, InterrogateService, UserControlService, with Windows' return codes; the Paused and pending states. Every value is read from the process or the service manager. DeviceID properties are spelled DeviceID. A number put into an integer parameter of another width is accepted; every CIM type reads back from a spawned instance.
